good afternoon everybody  i'm assistant sheriff andrew walsh and  i'm here to brief you on the additional  details as we know them today about the  officer involved shooting that occurred  on thursday august 11 2022  this is officer involved shooting number  seven for this year and it's the third  non-fatal officer-involved shooting  we've had so far in 2022. at the same  time last year we had five  officer-involved shootings and three of  those being non-fatal  this event was initiated as a follow-up  investigation on august 11th at 501 pm  before i get into the details of the  officer-involved shooting i wanted to  give you some backdrop to the history of  the follow-up investigation  on may 20th  of this year officers responded to a  violent carjacking that occurred in the  area of north los feliz street and  stewart avenue  during this robbery  a white male adult  stole a vehicle at gunpoint from a 73  year old female victim  officers then  identified the suspect and on the day of  the officer-involved shooting they were  conducting covert surveillance at his la  cover surveillance at his last known  address  and there were two separate locations  where officers discharged their weapon  during this officer-involved shooting  the first officer-involved shooting  occurred in the area of 5th street and  craig road which is located in north las  vegas  the second officer-involved shooting  location occurred at the 4800 block of  west desert inn road in las vegas which  is in this  spring valley area command and you can  see both of these areas depicted on the  screen and the maps to my left  there were five officers that were  involved in this officer-involved  shooting the first officer is officer  brendan burbrink he is 36 years old and  has been with the lvmpd since 2015.  in this incident officer burbrink was  armed with the smith and wesson m p nine  millimeter equipped with the tactical  light and the investigation revealed  that he fired eight rounds  the second officer involved is officer  christian maharo he is 27 years old and  has been with the lvmpd since 2021.  in this incident officer mahara was  armed with a glock 17 nine millimeter  equipped with the tactical light and the  investigation revealed that he fired  four rounds  the third officer involved in this  incident is officer alondra montero  she is 24 years old and has been with  the lvmpd since 2021.  in this incident officer montero was  armed with a glock 17 nine millimeter  equipped with the tactical light and the  investigation revealed that she fired  eight rounds  the fourth officer is officer amanda  montalto  she is 31 years old and has been with  the lvmpd since 2017.  in this incident officer montalto was  armed with a glock 19 nine millimeter  equipped with the tactical light and the  investigation revealed that she fired  eleven rounds during this incident and  the fifth officer involved in this  incident is officer mark sayus or  cesaius is 35 years old and has been  with the lvmpd since 2019  this investigation revealed that officer  says fired six rounds during this  incident and all the officers i just  named are assigned to the community  policing division and they all work at  the northeast area command in this  incident the suspect was identified as  justin lee venegas  justin is a forty year old white male  adult he's approximately five foot five  and weighs about 150 170 pounds and he  is pictured  on the screen to my left  and the investigation revealed that  during this incident venegas was armed  with a smith and wesson m p nine  millimeter pistol and he also used a  stolen white chevy avalanche as a weapon  when he intentionally rammed one of our  canine vehicles and the investigation  revealed that during this incident  office uh excuse me the suspect venegas  fired a total of four rounds now venegas  faces several charges stemming from the  officer involved shooting i'll read  those off to you now  venegas has been charged with three  counts three counts of attempted murder  with a deadly weapon on a protected  person one count of battery with a  deadly weapon on a protected person  one count of attempted murder with a  deadly weapon  one count of attempted robbery  one count of discharging a firearm at a  moving vehicle  one count of robbery with deadly weapon  and one count of felony evading  now stemming back to the may incident  venegas has been charged with robbery  with a deadly weapon with a victim over  sixty two counts of assault with a  deadly weapon with a victim over sixty  two counts of assault with a deadly  weapon  and grand larceny auto  now i'll give you the details for the  officer involved shooting  on august 11 2022 plainclothes officers  were conducting a follow-up  investigation at justin venegas's last  known address in the northeast part of  the valley  officers saw vanegas enter a vehicle and  drive out of the area  the air unit was requested to assist in  following venegas as he left the area  and drove away  while following venegas the air unit saw  him get out of his vehicle and point a  firearm at the driver of a white chevy  avalanche in the area of north pecos  road and cheyenne avenue and then  venegas while the air unit was watching  proceeded to carjack that vehicle and  drive away in the chevy avalanche  after the violent robbery at  approximately 7 13 pm patrol officers  tried to pull venegas over  the vehicle pursuit was initiated and  banegas failed to stop for the mock  patrol officers an unmarked lvmpd  vehicle became part of the pursuit and  that vehicle is equipped with police  lights and sirens and was behind the  venegas during this vehicle pursuit  venegas suddenly came to an abrupt stop  causing the unmarked police vehicle to  crash into the back of the stolen  vehicle  the collision disabled the police  vehicle and the officer was subsequently  transported to the hospital for minor  injuries mark patrol units continued to  pursue venegas and attempted a pit  maneuver in the area of craig road and  north fifth street and as you know from  previous incidents in previous press  briefings pitt stands for the precision  intervention technique and is designed  defined as a specific manner of  intentional contact using a police  vehicle against a fleeing vehicle during  a pursuit to cause the fleeing vehicle  to come to an abrupt stop rendering it  immobile  venegus avoided the fit the pit by  shooting at officers two times  from the with his firearm and striking  the windshield of the patrol vehicle  officer brendan burbrink who was a  passenger in the patrol vehicle fired  five rounds from his duty weapon through  the windshield  officer burbrink's rounds impacted the  rear of the stolen vehicle however  venegas was not struck  after the shooting venegus continued to  evade officers in the stolen vehicle  throughout the pursuit venegas drove  through red lights and displayed  reckless behavior as he drove around  congested areas of traffic and at times  his speeds would reach in excess of 100  miles per hour  as venegas approached the intersection  of desert inn road and jones boulevard  he forced the female motorist to a stop  he attempted to steal her vehicle by  jumping out of the white chevy avalanche  and ran towards her with the gun in his  hand attempting to get her out of her  vehicle the driver of this vehicle was  able to put her vehicle in reverse and  as she backed away vegas fired upon her  thankfully this victim of this attempted  robbery wasn't seriously hindered or  hurt by the gunfire and she was treated  at the scene by medical personnel and  released  venegas then ran back to the original  stolen chevy avalanche and fled  eastbound on desert inn as police  officers and marked vehicles attempted  to catch up with him a short time later  venegas drove into a busy grocery store  shopping center located at the 4800  block of west desert in road  again venegas attempted to carjack  another vehicl